00:33:52.000 --> 00:34:25.000
but bears out the general direction she's trying to push him in. Why do you think Chester Arthur listens to her? I do imagine that he is touched by anyone having faith in him. When what he is hearing from outside and inside is, this is bad, you're the worst person that we could have in this position. And that anyone believes he's capable of it, I think is a big thing. But also that Arthur at this point, he's a widower, his wife has been dead for a number of years. And the way that these letters are written, you can't help but read them as there's this delightful young woman who believes in me
但确实朝着她试图推动他的大致方向在前进。你认为切斯特·亚瑟为什么会听取她的意见？我猜想，当有人对抱有信心时，他内心一定深受触动。当时他在外界和内部听到的全都是：这很糟糕，你是在这个职位上我们能选出的最糟糕的人。而居然有人相信他有能力胜任，我认为这意义重大。但同时也是因为，当时的亚瑟是个鳏夫，他的妻子已经去世好几年了。从这些信件的字里行间，你会不由自主地感受到：这里有一位迷人的年轻女性，她相信我，

62
00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:37.000
and is speaking to me in a way that is intelligent and that is meaningful and when you're a man of a certain age who's interested in women to get a letter from a woman you've never met who is like, I believe in you, I think you can be great.
并且以一种既聪明又有意义的方式与我对话；当你是一个到了一定年纪、对女性感兴趣的男人时，能收到一封来自从未谋面的女子的信，信中说“我相信你，我认为你能成就伟大”，这种感觉……

