00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:51.000
Here's how to do it. It's written in this delightful way. I think it hit the bullseye of what he needed to hear at that moment and in a voice that he was eager to listen to or that was attractive to listen to. And I think if you read between the lines, you can kind of feel the possibility,
“该怎么做，请听我说。”信是以这种令人愉悦的方式写的。我认为它精准地击中了他在那个时刻最需要听到的心声，并且以一种他渴望倾听的、具有吸引力的声音表达了出来。我想如果你细细品味字里行间，你就能隐约感受到那种浪漫情愫的可能，

64
00:34:51.000 --> 00:35:15.000
of something romantic. Maybe Sand hopes for it. Maybe Arthur wonders about it. And at some point, he actually goes and visits her. Could you talk about that, what happened there and what led to that? So we only know about this from a letter that Julia writes to Arthur that's dated August 24, 1882. And she talks in it about how, she says at the start, she goes, my friend. My friend.
或许桑对此抱有期许，或许亚瑟也对此浮想联翩。而在某个时刻，他真的去拜访了她。你能谈谈这件事吗？当时发生了什么，又是什么促成了这次会面？我们对这件事的了解，仅来源于朱莉娅写给亚瑟的一封信，信的日期是1882年8月24日。她在信中谈到了他是如何……她在开头说道：我的朋友。我的朋友。

